Catalog: {
	GigaBarrelBomb: Hoists a large barrel and charges nearby ground enemies, dealing {0} damage in an 18×18-tile area; <cooldown>-second cooldown. Before upgrading, base damage rises to 480 in Hardmode. Automatically targets groups or grounded bosses; manual use also targets single enemies. Requires a safe ground route. Airborne use first finds a safe place to land; this can also happen automatically during combat. Cancelled charges do not spend the full cooldown. Does not damage tiles, players or your Palico.
	HoneyCage: Restores {0} life to you immediately, then another {1} life over 5 seconds. Triggers at 70% life or below when you are missing at least {2} life. <cooldown>-second cooldown. Works during Potion Sickness.
	GuardShield: Blocks one heavy hit against you, preventing up to {0} damage. <cooldown>-second cooldown. When you are above 70% life, it can instead protect your Palico at 35% life or below, or from a lethal hit. Both uses share a cooldown.
	CleansingPot: Removes one common debuff from you, such as Poisoned, On Fire! or Slow, prioritizing more harmful effects. Grants immunity to that debuff for {0} seconds afterward. <cooldown>-second cooldown. Minor debuffs about to expire do not trigger it. Does not remove Potion Sickness or Mana Sickness.
	CheerBell: Restores {0} mana to you or your Palico and reduces the recipient's mana cost by {1} for 6 seconds. <cooldown>-second cooldown. Prioritizes you when casting below half mana; otherwise helps your Palico while casting or waiting for mana. The recipient must be missing at least the restoration amount or half their maximum mana, whichever is lower.
	BattleDrum: Triggers when your Palico starts attacking: +{0} damage and +{1} attack speed for 10 seconds. <cooldown>-second cooldown. During the effect, your Palico's summons deal +{2} damage.
	PiercingBoomerang: On hit, you and your Palico gain {0} armor penetration against the target for {1} seconds. <cooldown>-second cooldown. Prioritizes stronger enemies and avoids targets with plenty of time left on this effect. Multiple applications do not stack.
	UpdraftBag: While you are airborne, unmounted and holding Jump with little flight time left, restores {0} seconds of flight. Without wings, gives you a small upward boost instead. <cooldown>-second cooldown.
	BombPot: Your Palico throws a bomb dealing {0} area damage in a 10×10-tile area. Before upgrading, base damage rises to 240 in Hardmode. <cooldown>-second cooldown. Does not destroy blocks. Aims ahead of moving targets and prioritizes nearby groups of visible enemies.
	PlunderKnife: Enemies damaged by you or your Palico can drop extra loot on defeat, regardless of the distance between you. Normal enemies have a {0} chance to drop 1 extra stackable loot item. Vanilla boss materials yield an average of {1} extra. Excludes Treasure Bags, unstackable items, coins, Hearts, Stars, biome keys, and normal enemies' Cyan-rarity or higher items. Does not trigger on friendly creatures or statue-spawned enemies. With multiple players, normal enemies use only the highest tier; boss bag materials are checked separately for each player.
	MiningKit: Your Palico mines {0} faster. Ore detection, digging assistance and pickaxe reach each extend by {1} tiles. Does not increase pickaxe power or change your own mining stats.
	GardenKit: Chopping trees or harvesting mature herbs with either you or your Palico yields extra resources, regardless of the distance between you. Average extra yield: {0} wood and {1} herbs, awarded at random. Does not increase seeds, gems or furniture drops, or apply to placed wood blocks. Your Palico gains {2} fishing power.
	ExpandedBelt: Permanently adds one Palico support slot. Can only be used once.
	ImprovedTools: Permanently upgrades Palico work and support gear to the Improved tier. Requires the Reinforced Toolkit first.
	MasterTools: Permanently upgrades Palico support and work gear to the Masterwork tier. Requires the Improved Toolkit first.
	CatWorkbench: Craft Palico gear, the Expanded Toolbelt and toolkit upgrades here. Right-click to open the Palico Guide.
	Basic: Basic
	Improved: Improved
	Masterwork: Masterwork
	IronBars: Iron / Lead Bars
	SilverBars: Silver / Tungsten Bars
	GoldBars: Gold / Platinum Bars
	SupportGear: Palico support gear
	WorkGear: Palico work gear
	CraftingStation: Palico crafting station
	PermanentUpgrade: Permanent Palico upgrade
	ActiveCondition: Active while equipped and your Palico is out; inactive while stowed, paused or recovering
	CurrentTier: "Current tier: "
	Legacy: Legacy modifications are now built in. Modification materials are refunded when this enters your inventory; the gear is kept.
	SupportSlotAdded: Support slots +1
	ReinforcedTools: Permanently upgrades Palico work and support gear to the Reinforced tier.
	CelestialTools: Permanently upgrades Palico work and support gear to the Celestial tier. Requires the Masterwork Toolkit first.
	Reinforced: Reinforced
	Celestial: Celestial
	CobaltBars: Cobalt / Palladium Bars
	ToolsUpgraded: Palico tools · {0}
	CelestialHealing: Celestial: for maximum life above 500, restores 1 extra life immediately per 10 points and 1 extra life over time per 50 points. All healing over time still finishes within 5 seconds. The missing-life threshold increases accordingly.
	CelestialPierce: Celestial: armor penetration scales with the current world's post-Moon Lord progress. Thorium's Primordials grant 18; Calamity's Providence, Polterghast, Devourer of Gods, Yharon, and Exo Mechs or Supreme Calamitas grant 18, 20, 24, 28, and 32 respectively. Only the highest milestone applies. Duration and cooldown are unchanged.
	CelestialShield: Celestial: blocks additional damage equal to 8% of the protected character's maximum life above 500, rounded down.
	CelestialMana: Celestial: restores 1 extra mana per 5 maximum mana above 200.
	CelestialDamage: Celestial: damage scales with the current world's post-Moon Lord progress. Thorium's Primordials grant ×1.5. Calamity's Providence, Polterghast, Devourer of Gods, Yharon, and Exo Mechs or Supreme Calamitas grant ×1.5, ×2, ×3, ×4, and ×6 respectively. Only the highest milestone applies.
}

Guide: {
	Saves:
		'''


		[Saving]
		Upgrades and gear stay with your character. Chest permissions are remembered separately for each world.
		'''
	AdvancedOrders:
		'''

		Advanced manual work orders are single-player only.
		'''
	Multiplayer:
		'''
		[Your own companion]
		Each player's inventory, upgrades and loadouts are saved separately. Each player chooses their attribute mode. Private chatter is only shown to the owner.

		[Settings and multiplayer]
		Personal options such as automatic work are set individually. The host or server administrator controls shared ability settings, including damage and inheritance ratios.
		The server and all players need this mod installed.
		'''
	RecipeBrowser:
		'''

		Recipe Browser also has a Palico gear category.
		'''
	Equipment:
		'''
		[Two attribute modes]
		Player-stat inheritance uses bonuses for the weapon's class at the configured ratios. Equipment trigger effects are not copied.
		Independent equipment uses the Palico's own armor, accessories and set effects, without stacking owner equipment bonuses. Base life and mana follow your permanent upgrades.
		Switch in Companion abilities. Armor and accessories are kept but inactive in inheritance mode.
		Both modes share your regular potion and station buffs by default; turn this off in Companion abilities. Food still needs to be fed to your Palico.

		[Armor and accessories]
		Independent equipment has 3 armor and 5 base accessory slots. Extra slots follow the owner's vanilla unlock rules. Active keybind skills are not automated; some modded effects still need integration.

		[Three loadouts]
		Weapons, armor, accessories, work and support gear are saved separately; dye is shared. Favorites are shared with matching empty slots in other loadouts. Unfavoriting keeps the item in the current loadout. Switching does not reset cooldowns.

		[Support slots and upgrades]
		The Expanded Toolbelt adds 1 support slot. Using a Demon Heart adds another in Expert or Master worlds. In Classic worlds, gear from the extra Expert slot returns to the backpack, or is held safely if full.
		Use Reinforced, Improved, Masterwork, then Celestial Toolkits to strengthen work and support gear. Some skill cooldowns also decrease. See Upgrades & crafting for recipes.
		'''
	Reserves:
		'''


		[Reserves and coins]
		Choose coin destinations and reserve amounts in settings. A reserve of 0 disables restocking, but existing supplies can still be used.
		Coin Gun ammunition is kept. Coins that do not fit in the Piggy Bank stay in the Palico inventory.
		'''
	MagicStorage:
		'''

		The cat icon beside Magic Storage grants access to the whole network. Restocking also works while its interface is open.
		'''
	Storage:
		'''
		[Transfers and favorites]
		With the panel open, Shift-click non-favorited items in your inventory or a chest to transfer them to your Palico.
		Backpack favorites stay put during bulk withdrawal but remain usable and consumable. Equipment favorites are shared between loadouts; see Equipment & growth.

		[Supply chests]
		Open a chest and click the cat icon to allow access. You can allow several chests. While you are nearby and the chest is closed, your Palico stores matching items and restocks consumables.
		'''
	Fishing:
		'''
		[Fishing]
		Give your Palico bait, then linger by water, cast your own line or direct them to a pool.
		Uses the best rod you carry and inherits your fishing bonuses, but consumes their own bait. Never uses Truffle Worms. Lava fishing still requires suitable gear or bait.
		Prefers stronger bait from its own inventory. Catches use native rolls with your biome, luck and Crate Potion effects. Quest fish already in the Palico inventory are not caught again.
		If the inventory is full, catches land on the ground. Clear them or make room to continue.

		[Critters]
		Catches nearby critters with a basic net, or a better net you carry.

		Work gear is optional. The Harvest Basket improves gathering yields and your Palico's fishing power.
		'''
	Exploring:
		'''
		[Collecting and sharing]
		Player-dropped items have a 10-second handoff window; a direct collection order bypasses it. Exclude unwanted items in settings, or put an Encumbering Stone in the Palico backpack to block ordinary pickups. Unlock it to resume.
		New loot tops up your existing stacks; usable Life Crystals and similar upgrades are handed over too. Your Palico keeps supplies first; favorited and manually stored items stay put.

		[Exploring and lighting]
		Points out Life Crystals, chests and other finds, and brings nearby Hearts or Stars when needed. Put Torches or Glowsticks in its backpack for light; holding them does not consume them.

		[Fly a kite]
		Hold a vanilla kite and right-click your idle Palico nearby. Hold left-click to let out line, right-click to reel in; switch items to finish.
		'''
	HarvestAndBuild:
		'''


		[Logging and herbs]
		Chops mature trees and harvests blooming herbs. Replants when seeds and space are available; gathering still works without seeds.

		[Building assistance]
		Can extend the platforms or ropes you are placing. Enable each in settings.
		'''
	QotMining:
		'''

		Quality of Terraria vein mining also applies to your Palico when enabled.
		'''
	Mining:
		'''
		[Digging and mining]
		Your Palico helps nearby while you swing a pickaxe, and gathers exposed ore and gems while idle.
		Uses the strongest pickaxe you carry, or a basic tool if you have none. If mining stalls, check pickaxe power and access. Exclude unwanted blocks in settings.
		The pickaxe button at the top of the panel pauses or resumes automatic digging, logging, planting and placement.
		'''
	Summons:
		'''


		[Minions and sentries]
		The slot beside the main weapon accepts a minion or sentry weapon. Your Palico returns to its main weapon after summoning or deploying. Replacing the summon weapon dismisses its summons.
		Limits follow the owner in inheritance mode, or the Palico's equipment and buffs in independent mode. Both have a minimum of 1 and do not use your own slots.
		Old One's Army weapons follow vanilla unlock rules. During the event, keep Etherian Mana in the Palico inventory.
		'''
	QotAmmo:
		'''

		With Quality of Terraria infinite ammo enabled, restocking accounts for the required stack size.
		'''
	Thorium:
		'''


		[Thorium class weapons]
		Instruments use separate inspiration, with base capacity following your permanent upgrades. It recovers when depleted; nearby allies receive native empowerments.
		Healing tools prioritize the injured owner and can heal nearby allies. Self-healing spells heal the Palico. Healing bonuses follow the attribute mode; the Palico pays its own mana and life costs.
		You can heal your Palico with ally-healing weapons, subject to their usual range and contact requirements.
		Throwing weapons retain native consumption and exhaustion, resting when overexerted.
		'''
	Combat:
		'''
		[Combat modes]
		Click the sword button to cycle modes. Proactive seeks nearby enemies. Assist attacks targets you hit or mark, and retaliates when you or your Palico are hit. Passive still allows work, pickup and healing.

		[Weapons and support]
		Equip throwing weapons as a stack. Keep ammo and potions in the Palico inventory. Support skills activate automatically or on request through their status-card icons; the Shield and Updraft Pouch are automatic only.

		[Recovery and fainting]
		Inheritance mode uses the configured share of your bonus regeneration, 50% by default. Independent equipment uses the Palico's own equipment and buff regeneration. Recovery timing follows its own injuries in both modes.
		Your Palico retreats when defeated and returns after recovering. With no boss or nearby threats, Calamity or Quality of Terraria fast-respawn rules can shorten the wait.
		'''
	DirectAndRecover:
		'''
		point at ore, a tree, dropped items or water and left-click.
		Tasks pause during combat. Recall cancels them; while following, moving away ends the current task.

		[Stay and follow]
		Click Stay here at the bottom of the panel to keep your Palico nearby for combat, pickup or fishing. Follow me or Recall brings it back; stowing it or entering a world also restores following.

		[Feeding]
		Hold vanilla food, such as cooked fish or fruit, and right-click your Palico nearby. One serving increases out-of-combat health regeneration by 25% for the food's usual duration. Neither the effect nor its duration stacks.
		'''
	Introduction:
		'''
		[Open the panel]
		Right-click your Palico nearby or click the status card. Click the portrait or name in the panel header to rename or recolor it; open Stats to see current bonuses.

		[Status card and controls]
		Hold Alt to drag the status card; reset its position in settings. Bind panel, recall, stow / call out and status-card keys in Controls. Gamepad controls are supported too.

		[Give a task]

		'''
	BindKey: "Assign the Direct companion key in Controls, then hold it and "
	HoldKey: "Hold "
	AfterKey: " and "
}

CompanionStatusBar.Vitals: "{0} · Life {1}/{2} · Mana {3}/{4}"

